w: * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
w: 2.~God will him keep, yea, save a- live; on earth he blessed shall live; And to his e- ne- mies' de- sire thou wilt him not up give.
w: 3.~God will give strength when he on bed of lang- ui- shing doth mourn; And in his sick- ness sore, O Lord, thou all his bed wilt turn.
w: 4.~I said, O Lord, do thou ex- tend thy mer- cy un- to me; O do thou heal my soul; for why? I have of- fen- ded thee.
w: 5.~Those that to me are e- ne- mies, of me do e- vil say, When shall he die, that so his name may per- ish quite a- way?
w: 6.~To see me if he comes, he speaks vain words: but then his heart Heaps mis- chief to it, which he tells, when forth he doth de- part.
w: 7.~My ha- ters joint- ly whi- spe- ring, 'gainst me my hurt de- vise. Mis- chief, say they, cleaves fast to him; he li'th, and shall not rise.
w: 8.~Yea, ev'n mine own fa- mil- iar friend, on whom I did re- ly, Who ate my bread, ev'n he his heel a- gainst me lift- ed high.
w: 9.~But, Lord, be mer- ci- ful to me, and up a- gain me raise, That I may just- ly them re- quite ac- cor- ding to their ways.
w: 10.~By this I know that cer- tain- ly I fa- vored am by thee; Be- cause my ha- teful e- ne- my tri- umphs not o- ver me.
w: 11.~But as for me, thou me u- phold'st in mine in- te- gri- ty; And me be- fore thy coun- ten- ance thou sett'st con- ti- nual- ly.
w: 12.~The Lord, the God of Is- ra- el, be blessed for ev- er then, From age to age e- ter- nal- ly. A- men, yea, and a- men.
